        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Severe aortic stenosis, TAVI or surgical valve replacement performed</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 80-year-old female patient, admitted due to symptomatic aortic valve stenosis. Upon admission, echocardiographic assessment confirmed severe aortic stenosis with significantly reduced valve area and elevated mean pressure gradient. Given her age and overall clinical profile, the interdisciplinary Heart Team evaluated surgical risk using EuroSCORE II, concluding that transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI) represented the preferred therapeutic approach. The procedure was performed successfully via transfemoral access without periprocedural complications. Post-interventional echocardiography demonstrated excellent prosthetic valve function with no relevant paravalvular leakage. The patient recovered well and was mobilized promptly. She is discharged in stable condition on dual antiplatelet therapy. Please arrange close follow-up including echocardiographic control within three months. Do not hesitate to contact us should any concerns arise.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Hospital course note"
                }
              ]
